obs This is the second time in one day a lap's own closing index-row prose has pushed the next reader over the 192-byte bound -- a row that summarizes rather than points costs the next lap a diagnosis-and-repair cycle every time it happens. Writing future rows terser from the start (name + counts, no restated adjective clauses) would spare the next cold run this exact red.
